\ Spitfire: the raid and the fighting. A model is a sketch in its own terms —
\ metres right, up and forward of its centre — drawn by carrying its points
\ through one more matrix product, from its own terms into the ground's, on
\ their way into the eye's. The Ju 88 A-1 and the He 111 H are built to their
\ published spans and lengths (20.08 m by 14.36 m, 22.60 m by 16.40 m), the
\ rest of their proportions estimated from drawings: fuselages of eight-sided
\ rings, the glazing, the gun positions and gondolas, tapered wings with
\ their hinge lines, round nacelles with three-blade propellers, the tail
\ surfaces with theirs, and the crosses.
\
\ A raid is bombers in vics of three, each following the one ahead of it: the
\ leader of each vic flies to the target at its speed and height, the others
\ station off its wings and behind; over the target they bomb, then turn for
\ home. An escort of Bf 110s fights until the bombers have bombed: each
\ takes the nearest Spitfire, the player's or the squadron's, breaks toward
\ it when it is behind, turns onto it within 3 km with the lead its rounds
\ need, and otherwise rejoins the bombers. The squadron's other Spitfires
\ break hard from a Bf 110 behind them and otherwise attack the nearest of
\ the raid. The turns are the Spitfire Mk I's 360° in 19 s at 12,000 ft
\ (RAE, published) and the Bf 110 C's 23.2 s, derived from it by the square
\ root of the wing loadings (175 kg/m² against 117), the wings taken to
\ reach the same greatest lift. Everything about the guns is gunnery.telic's;
\ an aircraft whose hits pass its strength smokes, rolls over and falls.

0xd0d0d0 constant bomber-colour
0x908070 constant smoke-colour

\ an engine on each wing: the nacelle as rings of six from its round cowling back past the wing, the propeller and its disc before it, six exhaust stubs down each side of the cowling; the stations are [ along radius ] from the cowling's face
: sketch-engines ( sketch out lift face stations propeller-radius -- )
	| sketch out lift face stations propeller-radius |
	stations ( station | [ station first face + station second station second lift ] ) map to rings
	stations second second to cowling
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		[ out side * 0 0 ] to centre
		sketch rings centre 6 sketch-body
		centre [ 0 lift face 0.15 + ] v+ to hub
		sketch hub propeller-radius sketch-propeller
		sketch hub propeller-radius sketch-propeller-disc
		[ -1 1 ] ( flank |
			0 6 1 do stub
				face 0.3 - stub 0.22 * - to along
				[ out side * flank cowling * + lift 0.15 + along ] to root
				sketch [ root root [ flank 0.1 * -0.03 -0.1 ] v+ ] sketch-path
			loop
		) each
	) each ;

\ the Balkenkreuz's outline: a cross of four arms, each a quarter as wide as the whole is long, on a plane given by two directions
: sketch-cross ( sketch centre across up size -- )
	| sketch centre across up size |
	size 2 / to reach
	reach 4 / to bar
	[ [ bar reach ] [ bar bar ] [ reach bar ] [ reach bar negate ] [ bar bar negate ] [ bar reach negate ]
	  [ bar negate reach negate ] [ bar negate bar negate ] [ reach negate bar negate ] [ reach negate bar ] [ bar negate bar ] [ bar negate reach ] ]
	( pair | centre across pair first v* v+ up pair second v* v+ ) map to corners
	sketch corners sketch-loop ;

\ the crosses: on each upper wing at a distance out, and on each side of the fuselage at a station
: sketch-crosses ( sketch wing-out wing-along wing-height wing-size side-out side-along side-height side-size -- )
	| sketch wing-out wing-along wing-height wing-size side-out side-along side-height side-size |
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		sketch [ wing-out side * wing-height wing-along ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 0 1 ] wing-size sketch-cross
		sketch [ side-out side * side-height side-along ] [ 0 0 1 ] [ 0 1 0 ] side-size sketch-cross
	) each ;

\ the Ju 88 A-1: a fuselage of nine rings; the glazed canopy raised over the crew's compartment with its frames and the two rear guns; the ventral gondola offset to starboard under the cockpit with its gun; tapered wings with rounded tips and the flaps' and ailerons' hinge line; the Jumo 211s in round cowlings with three-blade propellers; the tailplane, elevators, fin and rudder; the crosses. The span and length are published; every other figure is an estimate from drawings
: junkers-88 ( -- model )
	new-sketch to model
	model [ [ 7.1 0.15 0.15 0.05 ] [ 6.6 0.6 0.7 0.05 ] [ 5.6 0.85 1.0 0.1 ] [ 3.8 0.95 1.15 0.15 ] [ 1.5 0.9 1.05 0.05 ]
	        [ -1.5 0.8 0.9 0 ] [ -4 0.55 0.65 0.05 ] [ -6.6 0.3 0.4 0.15 ] [ -7.2 0.12 0.15 0.2 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	model [ [ -0.75 1.05 5.9 ] [ 0.75 1.05 5.9 ] [ 0.8 1.15 3.0 ] [ -0.8 1.15 3.0 ] ] sketch-loop
	model [ [ -0.5 1.75 5.2 ] [ 0.5 1.75 5.2 ] [ 0.55 1.8 3.3 ] [ -0.55 1.8 3.3 ] ] sketch-loop
	[ [ 0.75 1.05 5.9 0.5 1.75 5.2 ] [ 0.8 1.12 4.3 0.55 1.8 4.3 ] [ 0.8 1.15 3.0 0.55 1.8 3.3 ] ] ( bar |
		bar spread to top-along to top-up to top-out to foot-along to foot-up to foot-out
		[ -1 1 ] ( side |
			model [ [ foot-out side * foot-up foot-along ] [ top-out side * top-up top-along ] ] sketch-path
		) each
	) each
	model [ [ 0 1.75 5.2 ] [ 0 1.8 3.3 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ [ 0.25 1.65 3.2 ] [ 0.3 1.55 2.3 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ [ -0.25 1.65 3.2 ] [ -0.3 1.55 2.3 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ 0.3 -0.95 4.0 ] 0 0.7 2.4 0.5 sketch-box-centred
	model [ [ 0.3 -1.0 2.8 ] [ 0.3 -1.1 2.0 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ [ 0.9 2.0 ] [ 3.0 1.85 ] [ 8.5 0.9 ] [ 9.7 0.55 ] [ 10.04 0.0 ] [ 9.8 -0.6 ] [ 8.5 -0.95 ] [ 3.0 -1.5 ] [ 0.9 -1.8 ] ]
		[ [ [ 3.2 -1.15 ] [ 8.4 -0.6 ] ] [ [ 6.0 -1.2 ] [ 6.0 -0.82 ] ] ] 0.06 0 sketch-surface
	model 3.6 -0.05 3.7 [ [ 0 0.62 ] [ -0.7 0.7 ] [ -3.2 0.6 ] [ -4.7 0.45 ] [ -6.0 0 ] ] 1.7 sketch-engines
	model [ [ 0.5 -5.9 ] [ 3.0 -6.4 ] [ 3.7 -6.9 ] [ 3.5 -7.35 ] [ 0.5 -7.4 ] ] [ [ [ 0.5 -6.9 ] [ 3.6 -6.95 ] ] ] 0 0.2 sketch-surface
	model 0 [ [ -5.0 0.6 ] [ -6.3 2.9 ] [ -6.8 3.2 ] [ -7.5 3.0 ] [ -7.6 0.4 ] ] [ [ -6.9 3.1 ] [ -7.0 0.5 ] ] sketch-fin
	model [ [ 0 1.75 2.4 ] [ 0 2.15 2.2 ] [ 0 3.0 -6.8 ] ] sketch-path
	model 6.0 0.05 0.5 1.6 0.6 -3.5 0.05 1.2 sketch-crosses
	model bomber-colour sketch>object ;

\ the He 111 H: a fuselage of nine rings ending in the stepless glazed nose, its rear frame and the offset nose gun; the open dorsal gun position and its gun; the ventral gondola and its gun; wings with a swept leading edge, rounded tips and the hinge line; the Jumo 211s with three-blade propellers; the tail; the crosses. The span and length are published; every other figure is an estimate from drawings
: heinkel-111 ( -- model )
	new-sketch to model
	model [ [ 8.2 0.2 0.2 0 ] [ 7.8 0.65 0.7 0 ] [ 7.0 0.9 1.0 0.05 ] [ 5.5 1.0 1.2 0.1 ] [ 2.5 0.95 1.2 0.1 ]
	        [ -1.0 0.85 1.0 0.1 ] [ -4.0 0.6 0.75 0.1 ] [ -6.8 0.35 0.45 0.2 ] [ -8.2 0.15 0.2 0.25 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	model [ 6.4 0.95 1.1 0.07 ] [ 0 0 0 ] 8 body-ring sketch-loop
	model [ [ 0.2 0.2 8.0 ] [ 0.25 0.15 8.7 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ [ -0.35 1.05 -0.4 ] [ 0.35 1.05 -0.4 ] [ 0.35 1.0 -2.0 ] [ -0.35 1.0 -2.0 ] ] sketch-loop
	model [ [ 0 1.2 -1.2 ] [ 0 1.3 -2.6 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ 0 -1.3 1.5 ] 0 0.8 3.0 0.45 sketch-box-centred
	model [ [ 0 -1.3 0 ] [ 0 -1.45 -0.9 ] ] sketch-path
	model [ [ 1.0 2.4 ] [ 3.8 2.2 ] [ 8.0 1.2 ] [ 10.4 0.55 ] [ 11.3 -0.1 ] [ 10.8 -0.8 ] [ 8.0 -1.2 ] [ 3.8 -2.0 ] [ 1.0 -2.6 ] ]
		[ [ [ 4.0 -1.55 ] [ 10.4 -0.6 ] ] [ [ 7.2 -1.35 ] [ 7.2 -0.95 ] ] ] 0.044 0 sketch-surface
	model 3.8 -0.05 4.3 [ [ 0 0.62 ] [ -0.7 0.72 ] [ -3.8 0.62 ] [ -5.5 0.42 ] [ -6.6 0 ] ] 1.75 sketch-engines
	model [ [ 0.5 -6.6 ] [ 3.4 -7.2 ] [ 4.2 -7.8 ] [ 4.0 -8.4 ] [ 0.5 -8.6 ] ] [ [ [ 0.5 -8.0 ] [ 4.1 -8.05 ] ] ] 0 0.3 sketch-surface
	model 0 [ [ -6.1 0.6 ] [ -7.3 2.8 ] [ -7.9 3.3 ] [ -8.6 3.1 ] [ -8.7 0.5 ] ] [ [ -8.0 3.2 ] [ -8.1 0.6 ] ] sketch-fin
	model [ [ 0 1.2 -2.8 ] [ 0 1.65 -3.0 ] [ 0 3.2 -7.8 ] ] sketch-path
	model 7.5 0.0 0.45 1.8 0.58 -4.5 0.1 1.3 sketch-crosses
	model bomber-colour sketch>object ;

\ the Bf 110 C: a slim fuselage of eight rings; the long glazed canopy over the pilot and the gunner, its frames and the gunner's MG 15; the four MG 17s in the nose and the two MG FF cannon under it; tapered wings with the hinge line; the DB 601s in slim nacelles with three-blade propellers; the tailplane and the twin fins at its tips; the crosses. The span, length and height are published (16.25 m, 12.1 m, 3.5 m); every other figure is an estimate from drawings
: messerschmitt-110 ( -- model )
	new-sketch to model
	model [ [ 5.6 0.15 0.2 0 ] [ 5.3 0.45 0.55 0 ] [ 4.3 0.6 0.75 0.05 ] [ 2.5 0.62 0.85 0.15 ]
	        [ 0.0 0.6 0.85 0.15 ] [ -2.5 0.45 0.6 0.1 ] [ -5.0 0.25 0.35 0.15 ] [ -6.4 0.12 0.15 0.2 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	model [ [ -0.45 0.85 3.4 ] [ 0.45 0.85 3.4 ] [ 0.5 0.95 -1.2 ] [ -0.5 0.95 -1.2 ] ] sketch-loop
	model [ [ -0.32 1.45 2.8 ] [ 0.32 1.45 2.8 ] [ 0.32 1.4 -0.9 ] [ -0.32 1.4 -0.9 ] ] sketch-loop
	[ [ 0.45 0.85 3.4 0.32 1.45 2.8 ] [ 0.5 0.9 1.8 0.32 1.45 1.8 ] [ 0.5 0.92 0.6 0.32 1.42 0.6 ] [ 0.5 0.95 -1.2 0.32 1.4 -0.9 ] ] ( bar |
		bar spread to top-along to top-up to top-out to foot-along to foot-up to foot-out
		[ -1 1 ] ( side |
			model [ [ foot-out side * foot-up foot-along ] [ top-out side * top-up top-along ] ] sketch-path
		) each
	) each
	model [ [ 0 1.35 -1.0 ] [ 0 1.3 -2.0 ] ] sketch-path
	[ [ 0.12 0.35 ] [ -0.12 0.35 ] [ 0.12 0.15 ] [ -0.12 0.15 ] ] ( muzzle |
		model [ [ muzzle first muzzle second 5.4 ] [ muzzle first muzzle second 6.2 ] ] sketch-path
	) each
	[ -1 1 ] ( side |
		model [ [ side 0.15 * -0.55 3.8 ] [ side 0.15 * -0.6 4.8 ] ] sketch-path
	) each
	model [ [ 0.6 1.7 ] [ 3.0 1.55 ] [ 7.4 0.8 ] [ 8.0 0.55 ] [ 8.125 0.1 ] [ 8.0 -0.4 ] [ 7.4 -0.55 ] [ 3.0 -1.15 ] [ 0.6 -1.4 ] ]
		[ [ [ 3.2 -0.85 ] [ 7.4 -0.3 ] ] [ [ 5.3 -0.84 ] [ 5.3 -0.6 ] ] ] 0.05 0 sketch-surface
	model 2.4 -0.05 3.4 [ [ 0 0.45 ] [ -0.6 0.55 ] [ -2.8 0.48 ] [ -4.2 0.3 ] [ -5.0 0 ] ] 1.65 sketch-engines
	model [ [ 0.3 -5.0 ] [ 2.8 -5.3 ] [ 3.2 -5.6 ] [ 3.2 -6.3 ] [ 0.3 -6.4 ] ] [ [ [ 0.3 -5.9 ] [ 3.2 -5.95 ] ] ] 0 0.25 sketch-surface
	[ -3.15 3.15 ] ( out |
		model out [ [ -5.2 -0.8 ] [ -5.0 0.9 ] [ -5.4 1.4 ] [ -6.2 1.45 ] [ -6.6 0.9 ] [ -6.5 -0.7 ] ] [ [ -6.0 1.4 ] [ -6.0 -0.7 ] ] sketch-fin
	) each
	model [ [ 0 1.42 -1.3 ] [ 0 1.8 -1.5 ] [ 3.15 1.4 -5.9 ] ] sketch-path
	model 5.5 0.0 0.4 1.2 0.42 -3.0 0.12 1.0 sketch-crosses
	model bomber-colour sketch>object ;

variable models
{ } to models
variable bombers
[ ] to bombers

variable far-models
{ } to far-models

\ the drogue: a cloth sleeve 6 m long, 1 m across at its mouth and 0.7 m at its tail (estimates), on a bridle of four lines meeting 2 m ahead of the mouth
: drogue-model ( -- model )
	new-sketch to model
	model [ [ 3 0.5 0.5 0 ] [ -3 0.35 0.35 0 ] ] [ 0 0 0 ] 8 sketch-body
	[ [ 0.5 0 3 ] [ -0.5 0 3 ] [ 0 0.5 3 ] [ 0 -0.5 3 ] ] ( corner | model [ corner [ 0 0 5 ] ] sketch-path ) each
	model bomber-colour sketch>object ;

\ a box in a model's own terms, between two values on each axis: its two ends' outlines and the four edges joining them
: sketch-block ( sketch x0 x1 y0 y1 z0 z1 -- )
	| sketch x0 x1 y0 y1 z0 z1 |
	[ y0 y1 ] ( y | sketch [ [ x0 y z0 ] [ x1 y z0 ] [ x1 y z1 ] [ x0 y z1 ] ] sketch-loop ) each
	[ [ x0 z0 ] [ x1 z0 ] [ x1 z1 ] [ x0 z1 ] ] ( corner | sketch [ [ corner first y0 corner second ] [ corner first y1 corner second ] ] sketch-path ) each ;

\ HMS Glorious as in 1940, from her waterline's centre: 239.8 m long overall and 27.6 m in the beam at the waterline (published); the hull to a deck 10 m above the water; the flight deck 18 m above the water over two hangars each 4.9 m high (published), 185 m long from 110 m aft of the centre and 28 m wide; its two lifts 14.0 by 14.6 m (published), fore and aft; the island on the starboard side with the bridge, the funnel and the mast (heights, the flight deck's ends and the lifts' places estimates)
: carrier-model ( -- model )
	new-sketch to model
	[ [ 0 120 ] [ 9 95 ] [ 13.8 60 ] [ 13.8 -80 ] [ 11 -112 ] [ 0 -120 ] [ -11 -112 ] [ -13.8 -80 ] [ -13.8 60 ] [ -9 95 ] ] to plan
	[ 0 10 ] ( up | model plan ( corner | [ corner first up corner second ] ) map sketch-loop ) each
	plan ( corner | model [ [ corner first 0 corner second ] [ corner first 10 corner second ] ] sketch-path ) each
	model -14 14 18 18 -110 75 sketch-block
	[ [ -14 -110 ] [ 14 -110 ] [ -14 75 ] [ 14 75 ] [ -14 -20 ] [ 14 -20 ] ] ( corner | model [ [ corner first 10 corner second ] [ corner first 18 corner second ] ] sketch-path ) each
	[ 50 -75 ] ( along | model -7 7 18 18 along 7.3 - along 7.3 + sketch-block ) each
	-100 70 10 do along
		model [ [ 0 18 along ] [ 0 18 along 5 + ] ] sketch-path
	loop
	model 12 16 18 30 -5 25 sketch-block
	model 12.5 15.5 30 38 -2 8 sketch-block
	model [ [ 14 30 15 ] [ 14 46 15 ] ] sketch-path
	model bomber-colour sketch>object ;

\ each type's model near and from afar, the far ones from the published spans and lengths and the engines' distance out; the Spitfire's and the Hurricane's with wheels up and down; the Lysander target tug's from afar only, its published 50 ft span and 30 ft 6 in length
: build-models ( -- )
	| ^models ^far-models |
	{ :ju-88 junkers-88 :he-111 heinkel-111 :bf-110 messerschmitt-110
	  :spitfire false spitfire-model :spitfire-down true spitfire-model
	  :hurricane false hurricane-model :hurricane-down true hurricane-model
	  :lysander 15.24 9.3 0 bomber-colour far-model :drogue drogue-model :carrier carrier-model } to models
	{ :ju-88 20.08 14.36 3.6 bomber-colour far-model :he-111 22.6 16.4 3.8 bomber-colour far-model
	  :bf-110 16.25 12.1 2.4 bomber-colour far-model :spitfire 11.23 9.12 0 spitfire-colour far-model
	  :hurricane 12.19 9.55 0 spitfire-colour far-model
	  :lysander models@lysander :drogue models@drogue :carrier models@carrier } to far-models
	far-models far-models@spitfire :spitfire-down ! drop
	far-models far-models@hurricane :hurricane-down ! drop ;

\ === moving models ===

\ the matrix that takes a model's [ x y z 1 ] rows to the ground's, at a position and attitude
: model-matrix ( position attitude -- matrix )
	| position attitude |
	[ attitude@right spread 0 attitude@up spread 0 attitude@forward spread 0 position spread 1 ] 4 4 matrix ;

\ draw a model at a position and attitude in the bombers' colour for the time of day, unless behind the eye or beyond the visibility
: draw-model ( model position attitude -- )
	| model position attitude |
	position eye@position v- to offset
	offset eye@attitude@forward v-dot to ahead
	ahead -30 < if exit then
	offset v-length visibility > if exit then
	model@points position attitude model-matrix camera matmul matmul model@edges bomber-ink draw-edges ;

\ === the raid ===

\ an attitude facing a heading, climbing at a pitch and banked, all in degrees
: flying-attitude ( heading pitch bank -- attitude )
	| heading pitch bank |
	heading heading-attitude :right pitch PI 180 / * negate turn-attitude :forward bank PI 180 / * negate turn-attitude ;

\ a raid: vics of three from a starting point toward a target, at a height and speed
: new-raid ( kind n-vics start target height speed -- )
	| kind n-vics start target height speed ^bombers |
	target start v- heading-of to course
	[ ] to bombers
	0 n-vics 1 do vic
		0 3 1 do wing
			[ 0 -45 45 ] wing @i to out
			start course out 0 vic 250 * negate out abs 0.8 * - placed [ 0 height vic 40 * + 0 ] v+ to position
			bombers
			{ :kind kind :position position :heading course :pitch 0 :bank 0 :speed speed
			  :attitude course 0 0 flying-attitude
			  :height height vic 40 * + :target target :state :inbound :hits 0
			  :smoke [ ] :smoke-left 0 }
			add-last! drop
		loop
	loop ;

\ the bearing and distance to the raid's nearest living bomber from a point, for the controller's vector
: raid-vector ( point -- bearing distance )
	| point |
	bombers ( bomber | bomber@state :inbound = bomber@state :outbound = or ) filter to flying
	flying size 0 = if null null exit then
	flying ( bomber | bomber@position point v- v-length ) sort-by first to nearest
	nearest@position point v- to offset
	offset heading-of offset v-length ;

\ turn a bomber toward a heading at no more than 3° a second, banking with the turn
: steer-bomber ( bomber heading dt -- )
	| bomber heading dt |
	heading bomber@heading - 540 + 360 mod 180 - to error
	error -3 dt * 3 dt * clamp to turn
	bomber@heading turn + 360 + 360 mod bomber!heading
	turn dt / 10 * -30 30 clamp bomber!bank ;

\ the escort fighters: the most they turn, degrees a second, 360° in the derived 23.2 s; the most they pitch, degrees a second, and the speed they cruise at, m/s (estimates); the speed they fight at, the published 349 mph at 7,000 m
360 23.2 / constant fighter-turn-rate
20 constant fighter-pitch-rate
130 constant fighter-cruise-speed
156 constant fighter-top-speed

\ the squadron's other Spitfires: the most they turn, degrees a second, 360° in the RAE's 19 s; the speed they fight at, m/s (an estimate, above the Bf 110's as the Rechlin trial found)
360 19 / constant wingman-turn-rate
160 constant wingman-top-speed

variable wingmen
[ ] to wingmen

\ whether one of the raid is an escort fighter
: fighter? ( bomber -- flag ) :role :bomber @or :fighter = ;

\ whether an aircraft is the air-firing exercise's tug or drogue, flown by air-firing.telic and never brought down
: practice-target? ( craft -- flag )
	:role :bomber @or to role
	role :tug = role :drogue = or ;

\ whether an aircraft of the raid or the squadron is still in the air and fighting
: flying? ( craft -- flag )
	| craft |
	craft@state to state
	state :inbound = state :outbound = or state :flying = or ;

\ an aircraft's velocity, from its attitude and speed
: craft-velocity ( craft -- velocity )
	| craft |
	craft@attitude@forward craft@speed v* ;

\ the Spitfires the escort can attack: the player's and the squadron's still flying, each [ position velocity wingman ], the wingman null for the player's
: spitfire-targets ( -- targets )
	[ [ plane@position plane@velocity null ] ]
	wingmen ( wingman | wingman flying? ) filter ( wingman | [ wingman@position wingman craft-velocity wingman ] ) map concat ;

\ how a point lies from an aircraft: ahead along its nose, and off that line as a share of the distance ahead
: bearing-from ( craft point -- ahead off-line )
	| craft point |
	craft@attitude point craft@position v- ground>attitude spread to ahead to rising to across
	ahead
	across sq rising sq + sqrt ahead abs 1 max2 / ;

\ fly an aircraft toward a heading, a pitch and a speed: turning at no more than its rate and banking with the turn, pitching at no more than 20° a second, gaining speed diving and losing it climbing
: fly-at ( craft wanted-heading wanted-pitch wanted-speed turn-rate dt -- )
	| craft wanted-heading wanted-pitch wanted-speed turn-rate dt |
	craft@position second 400 < if wanted-pitch 20 max2 to wanted-pitch then
	wanted-heading craft@heading - 540 + 360 mod 180 - to error
	error turn-rate dt * negate turn-rate dt * clamp to turn
	craft@heading turn + 360 + 360 mod craft!heading
	turn dt / PI 180 / * craft@speed * gravity / atan 180 PI / * -75 75 clamp craft!bank
	wanted-pitch craft@pitch - fighter-pitch-rate dt * negate fighter-pitch-rate dt * clamp craft@pitch + craft!pitch
	wanted-speed craft@speed - 0.15 * craft@pitch PI 180 / * sin gravity * - dt * craft@speed + 60 200 clamp craft!speed ;

\ the heading and pitch toward an offset, the pitch held within limits
: heading-and-pitch ( towards lowest highest -- heading pitch )
	| towards lowest highest |
	towards heading-of
	towards second towards v-length 1 max2 / -1 1 clamp asin 180 PI / * lowest highest clamp ;

\ one escort fighter's choice and turn: it takes the nearest Spitfire; with that Spitfire behind it within 700 m it breaks toward it, diving; within 3 km it turns onto the Spitfire's course ahead, leading it by the rounds' flight; both at its top speed; farther off it rejoins the bombers, 400 m above the first still inbound, at its cruising speed; it climbs away from the ground under 400 m. With every bomber bombed or down it turns for home
: steer-fighter ( fighter dt -- )
	| fighter dt |
	bombers ( other | other fighter? not other@state :inbound = and ) filter to escorted
	escorted size 0 = if
		:outbound fighter!state
		exit
	then
	spitfire-targets ( target | target first fighter@position v- v-length ) sort-by first to chosen
	chosen first fighter@position v- to offset
	offset v-length to range
	fighter chosen first bearing-from drop to ahead
	range 3000 < if fighter-top-speed else fighter-cruise-speed then to wanted-speed
	range 700 < ahead 0 < and if
		offset heading-of to wanted-heading
		-15 to wanted-pitch
	else
		range 3000 < if
			chosen first chosen second range 800 / v* v+ fighter@position v- -35 35 heading-and-pitch to wanted-pitch to wanted-heading
		else
			escorted first to leader
			leader@position [ 0 400 0 ] v+ fighter@position v- -20 20 heading-and-pitch to wanted-pitch to wanted-heading
		then
	then
	fighter wanted-heading wanted-pitch wanted-speed fighter-turn-rate dt fly-at ;

\ whether an escort fighter's nose points within 15° of an aircraft within a distance (15° an estimate)
: points-at? ( enemy craft distance -- flag )
	| enemy craft distance |
	enemy fighter? not if false exit then
	enemy craft@position bearing-from to off-line to ahead
	ahead 0 > ahead distance < and off-line 0.27 < and ;

\ one of the squadron's Spitfires: with a Bf 110's nose pointing within 15° of it inside 1,000 m, from behind or ahead, it breaks, turning hard to the Bf 110's side 90° off its heading and diving, a turn the Bf 110 cannot follow; otherwise it turns onto the nearest of the raid not pointing at it within 3 km, leading it by the rounds' flight; with the raid gone it flies on level
: steer-spitfire ( wingman dt -- )
	| wingman dt |
	bombers ( enemy | enemy flying? ) filter to enemies
	enemies size 0 = if
		wingman wingman@heading 0 wingman-top-speed wingman-turn-rate dt fly-at
		exit
	then
	enemies ( enemy | enemy wingman 1000 points-at? ) filter to threats
	enemies ( enemy | enemy wingman 3000 points-at? not ) filter to quarries
	threats size 0 > quarries size 0 = or if
		enemies ( enemy | enemy@position wingman@position v- v-length ) sort-by first to threat
		wingman@attitude threat@position wingman@position v- ground>attitude first to across
		wingman@heading across 0 < if -90 else 90 then + to wanted-heading
		-10 to wanted-pitch
	else
		quarries ( enemy | enemy@position wingman@position v- v-length ) sort-by first to quarry
		quarry@position wingman@position v- v-length to range
		quarry@position quarry craft-velocity range 800 / v* v+ wingman@position v- -35 35 heading-and-pitch to wanted-pitch to wanted-heading
	then
	wingman wanted-heading wanted-pitch wingman-top-speed wingman-turn-rate dt fly-at ;

\ one bomber's step: fly its course, bomb the target, turn for home, or fall; an escort fighter fights until the bombers have bombed
: move-bomber ( bomber dt -- )
	| bomber dt |
	bomber practice-target? if exit then
	bomber@state to state
	state :down = if exit then
	state :falling = if
		bomber@pitch dt 12 * - -70 max2 bomber!pitch
		bomber@bank dt 40 * + bomber!bank
		bomber@speed dt 6 * + 160 min2 bomber!speed
	else bomber fighter? state :inbound = and if
		bomber dt steer-fighter
	else bomber :role :bomber @or :spitfire = if
		bomber dt steer-spitfire
	else
		bomber@target bomber@position v- to to-target
		[ to-target first 0 to-target 2 @i ] v-length to remaining
		state :inbound = remaining 600 < and if :outbound bomber!state true :bombed game! then
		bomber@state :inbound = if
			bomber to-target heading-of dt steer-bomber
		else
			bomber 80 dt steer-bomber
		then
		bomber@height bomber@position second - 0.05 * -0.3 0.3 clamp asin 180 PI / * bomber!pitch
	then then then
	bomber@heading bomber@pitch bomber@bank flying-attitude to attitude
	bomber attitude :attitude ! drop
	bomber bomber@position attitude@forward bomber@speed dt * v* v+ :position ! drop
	bomber@state :falling = if
		bomber@smoke-left dt - bomber!smoke-left
		bomber@smoke-left 0 <= if
			bomber@smoke bomber@position add-last! drop
			0.25 bomber!smoke-left
		then
		bomber@position first bomber@position 2 @i ground-height bomber@position second >= if
			:down bomber!state
			bomber :role :bomber @or :spitfire = if "A SPITFIRE HAS CRASHED" else "A RAIDER HAS CRASHED" then say
		then
	then ;

\ the damage taking hold: past 100 the engine stops
: suffer-damage ( -- )
	plane@damage 100 >= plane@engine-dead not and if
		true plane!engine-dead
		0 plane!throttle
		"ENGINE HIT - IT HAS STOPPED - GLIDE DOWN" say
	then ;

\ === drawing ===

\ one bomber and its smoke
: draw-bomber ( bomber -- )
	| bomber |
	bomber@state :down = not if
		bomber@position eye@position v- v-length far-distance > if far-models else models then
		bomber@kind @ bomber@position bomber@attitude draw-model
	then
	bomber@smoke size 1 > if
		new-sketch to trail
		trail bomber@smoke [ bomber@position ] concat sketch-path
		trail smoke-colour sketch>object draw-object
	then ;

\ every bomber and its smoke
: draw-raid ( -- ) bombers ( bomber | bomber draw-bomber ) each ;

\ the raid's step: the bombers, the escort and the squadron fly, and the damage takes hold; the guns are gunnery.telic's
: advance-raid ( dt -- )
	| dt |
	dt 0 <= if exit then
	bombers ( bomber | bomber dt move-bomber ) each
	wingmen ( wingman | wingman dt move-bomber ) each
	suffer-damage ;

\ === the missions ===

\ a raid's plan: the bomber, the vics of three, where they start, what they bomb, their height and speed
: raid-plan ( kind n-vics start target height speed -- plan )
	| kind n-vics start target height speed |
	{ :kind kind :n-vics n-vics :start start :target target :height height :speed speed } ;

\ the cruisers' anchorage, 2 km east of the Forth Bridge
: forth-anchorage ( -- point )
	:inchgarvie :north-queensferry landmark-heading 90 + to east-of-bridge
	:inchgarvie landmark-ground east-of-bridge 0 0 2000 placed ;

\ the missions, each a name, three lines of story, the Spitfire's start as [ position heading speed on-ground ], the raid's plan or null, night or day, whether it begins on the approach with wheels and flaps down, the propeller (the two-pitch in 1939, the constant-speed fitted from June 1940) and whether 100-octane fuel allows emergency boost (from 1940), the weather (the visibility in metres, the share of the sky's squares holding a cloud and the clouds' base, the wind as [ the bearing it blows from, metres a second ], every wind an estimate: the records found give none), the carrier's flight deck where the mission has one (Glorious's 28 knots, 14.4 m/s, and the 12-knot wind together giving the 40 knots over her deck published for 7 June; the split and the place, 40 km north of Andenes where she and Ark Royal were operating, estimates), any ballast the aircraft carries as [ kg place ] (the Glorious Hurricanes' published 15 lb sandbag, 6.8 kg, in the rear fuselage, its place an estimate), the aircraft where the mission fixes it (the PR Spitfire, or the Hurricane at Narvik and at Scapa Flow, where no Spitfires served; the Scapa raid's coming from the east about 7 pm, seen by the Shetland radar, published, its fifteen bombers, height and course estimates, the published counts running from 15 to 35, and drawn in daylight, the game having no dusk), the opening message, the group the title lists it under, and the briefing's text; over Norway the height the snow lay down to (estimates: Trøndelag's lowland under snow in early March, the thaw at Narvik begun on 29 April 1940 by the despatches, the snow then lying above about 400 m at the end of May and 600 m in June)
: missions ( -- missions )
	:turnhouse landmark-ground 60 0 wheel-height -580 placed to turnhouse-runway
	:abbotsinch :greenock landmark-heading to west-from-abbotsinch
	:dumbarton-castle :greenock landmark-heading to west-from-dumbarton
	:greenock landmark-ground to greenock
	forth-anchorage to anchorage
	:farne-islands landmark-ground 90 0 5200 8000 placed to farne-fight
	farne-fight 70 0 -600 2500 placed to heinkels
	:inchkeith :bass-rock landmark-heading to firing-course
	:inchkeith landmark-ground firing-course 0 1524 3000 placed to tug-start
	:bardufoss landmark-ground 100 0 :bardufoss landmark-height wheel-height + -580 placed to bardufoss-runway
	narvik-anchorage :narvik :vaernes landmark-heading 0 0 90000 placed to narvik-raid-start
	:andenes landmark-ground 0 0 0 40000 placed to glorious-centre
	:scapa-flow landmark-ground to scapa-anchorage
	scapa-anchorage 0 0 2500 -15000 placed to scapa-patrol
	[ { :name "THE FORTH, 16 OCTOBER 1939" :month 10
